      "writtenOn": "2025-05-06T17:02:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "on a 2nd though: looks like we shouldn\u0027t be caching it, esp over deep sleep.\nPCR0 is allowed to be extended only once per AP boot. each time a PCR0 value might be different (sometimes we try booting in normal, sometimes in recovery). so we shouldn\u0027t cache the checked_fwmp_ec_reset status from the previous AP boot. and caching it within the same AP boot is not needed: PCR0 is extended only once.\n\nadditionally, trying to boot in an unallowed mode should be rare. it\u0027s ok to take time and calculate everything when it happens.\n\nso, I suggest just dropping `static` and starting with `int checked_fwmp_ec_reset \u003d 0;` every time. which also means no need for early return check `if (checked_fwmp_ec_reset) return checked_fwmp_ec_reset \u003d\u003d FWMP_RESETS_EC_IN_REC_DEV;`",
      "parentUuid": "01ca361b_6c6a5ecf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "9200ea2d4d879c19179e0372ac398501bd5c0b8b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
