      "writtenOn": "2025-05-05T22:52:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "shouldn\u0027t this be first? only apply all other checks if the current PCR may require triggering EC_RST. and then all other checks to follow (that FWMP is actually blocking dev mode and that this particular board id requires reset).\n\nso the entire new logic shall be\n\n```\n#ifdef CONFIG_FWMP_BLOCK_REC_DEV_RESET_EC\nif (pcr_config_enabled(PCR_FWMP_BLOCK_DEV_TRIGGER_ECRST)\n    \u0026\u0026 !board_fwmp_allows_boot_policy_update()\n    \u0026\u0026 board_id_fwmp_resets_ec_in_rec_dev()) {\n        CPRINTS(\"pcr: block rec+dev\");\n        board_reboot_ec();\n}\n#endif\n```\n\notherwise, keeping it at the top-level in _plat__PCRUpdated() will confuse us if we add more actions on PCR changes (and it\u0027s likely we\u0027ll have more actions on PCR10 changes in the future).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 349,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 349,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "9200ea2d4d879c19179e0372ac398501bd5c0b8b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da0b1343_0ea1a7f9",
        "filename": "board/cr50/tpm2/platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 349,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-06T12:49:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I ordered the checks shortest check to longest check since this is going to happen every boot.\n\nIf pcr_config_enabled is checked first, then every board will have to check the entire PCR0 value against the known hashes every time pcr0 is updated.\n\nboard_id_fwmp_resets_ec_in_rec_dev caches it\u0027s value, so checking it first is very quick.",
      "parentUuid": "2010c7b9_83d61e05",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 349,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 349,
        "endChar": 60
      },
      "revId": "9200ea2d4d879c19179e0372ac398501bd5c0b8b",
